# hash-bench runtime dependencies.
#
# NOT the source of `requirements_lock_3_11.txt`. That lock is copied verbatim
# from the `hash_frx` commit `MODULE.bazel` pins, because a bzlmod consumer
# resolves each module's pip dependencies from its own lock and only EQUAL
# versions keep one frx and one zk_dtypes on a test's `sys.path`. Compiling a
# lock from this file would pick the newest frx satisfying the floor and put two
# of them in the runfiles tree. So there is deliberately no `requirements.update`
# target here: bumping the pin means copying that commit's lock over ours.
#
# This file records what hash-bench itself imports, so a reader can see which of
# the locked closure is ours and which arrives for hash_frx.
absl-py
numpy
frx
frxlib
frx-cuda12-pjrt
frx-cuda12-plugin
zk-dtypes
